WEBVTT

00:43.043 --> 00:45.713
CHAPTER 4:
STARS ARE BORN OUT OF CHAOS

00:45.796 --> 00:47.256
-Jeon Ji-min.
-Here!

00:48.758 --> 00:50.217
-Oh Ji-ho.
-Here!

00:50.801 --> 00:51.761
-Kim Ga-yeong.
-Here!

00:51.844 --> 00:54.680
He's taking attendance
before introducing himself?

00:54.764 --> 00:56.056
Who does he think he is?

00:56.140 --> 00:56.974
Kim Dan-ji.

00:58.184 --> 00:59.393
Here!

00:59.477 --> 01:01.061
-Kim Yeong-jae.
-Here!

01:02.021 --> 01:03.355
-Eun Ha-su.
-Here.

01:07.067 --> 01:08.903
I hear you won gold at the KMO?

01:10.279 --> 01:11.155
Yes.

01:11.238 --> 01:12.198
KMO?

01:12.823 --> 01:14.033
What's that?

01:14.116 --> 01:14.950
No idea.

01:15.034 --> 01:16.285
How was it?

01:18.287 --> 01:19.371
Not that difficult.

01:19.955 --> 01:22.666
Why is he talking to her
and only calling others' names?

01:23.417 --> 01:25.127
Are they best friends or something?

01:26.670 --> 01:27.797
-Oh A-rin.
-Here.

01:28.798 --> 01:30.132
-Choi Yu-mi.
-Here.

01:31.258 --> 01:32.468
-Yeo Eui-ju.
-Here.

01:39.099 --> 01:40.518
-Yeo Eui-ju?
-Here.

01:42.436 --> 01:44.063
-Yeo Eui-ju!
-Here!

01:49.860 --> 01:51.570
-Choi Go-ya.
-Here.

01:52.071 --> 01:52.947
Choi Ji-a.

01:58.160 --> 01:59.578
Choi Ji-a?

01:59.662 --> 02:00.496
Here.

02:08.712 --> 02:11.841
I am Mr. Ga, your new homeroom teacher.

02:11.924 --> 02:13.634
-So handsome!
-So handsome!

02:22.476 --> 02:24.645
Math is a discipline
that knows no falsehood.

02:25.354 --> 02:27.273
Euclid's Elements begins like this.

02:27.356 --> 02:29.650
"A point is that which has no part."

02:30.693 --> 02:31.777
Isn't that beautiful?

02:34.530 --> 02:35.823
Points connect to form lines.

02:35.906 --> 02:37.408
Lines move to create planes.

02:37.491 --> 02:39.702
Planes form boundaries that make solids.

02:39.785 --> 02:40.619
And solids

02:40.703 --> 02:42.538
exist within time and space.

02:42.621 --> 02:43.539
In other words,

02:44.373 --> 02:47.001
math is the language that explains
how the universe exists.

02:47.626 --> 02:49.712
That's why to understand mathematics

02:49.795 --> 02:52.172
is to understand the universe
you were born into.

02:57.845 --> 03:00.222
I think of you as stars in that universe.

03:00.848 --> 03:03.183
Each of you shining,
each with your own world.

03:05.102 --> 03:06.437
When a star is born,

03:06.520 --> 03:08.480
countless clouds of dust
surround it so densely

03:08.564 --> 03:10.065
you can't even see an inch ahead.

03:10.149 --> 03:11.275
That's why people say

03:12.359 --> 03:14.361
stars are born out of chaos.

03:17.239 --> 03:18.449
You're probably the same.

03:18.532 --> 03:20.618
-Oh, that's so deep.
-How cool is that?

03:20.701 --> 03:21.619
In the midst of that chaos,

03:21.702 --> 03:24.330
some of you may have figured out
what you like, what you don't,

03:24.997 --> 03:27.416
what you're good at
and what you want to do.

03:27.499 --> 03:28.834
But for those that haven't,

03:29.752 --> 03:31.045
I hope the rest of this semester

03:31.128 --> 03:33.130
will be the time you find it.

03:36.467 --> 03:38.177
If you're having difficulty,
I'll help you.

03:41.263 --> 03:42.723
But it must be you yourself

03:43.349 --> 03:45.351
that takes that final step.

03:47.937 --> 03:49.772
What the heck?

03:49.855 --> 03:52.691
All that guff about stars
and the universe to say that?

03:52.775 --> 03:54.151
His pride in math is unbelievable.

03:54.234 --> 03:55.653
What a nerdy math geek.

03:57.154 --> 03:58.113
Yeo Eui-ju.

03:59.365 --> 04:00.491
Yes, sir.

04:00.574 --> 04:02.993
What score did you get in math
in the last mock exam?

04:03.786 --> 04:05.871
Why is he asking that out of the blue?

04:07.081 --> 04:08.248
It was…

04:08.832 --> 04:10.000
I can't hear you.

04:11.543 --> 04:12.795
Four…

04:12.878 --> 04:13.712
Forty…

04:16.006 --> 04:17.216
Four points, sir.

04:24.056 --> 04:25.182
Four points?

04:28.143 --> 04:29.103
If that's all you got…

04:35.025 --> 04:37.403
you ought to go back to grade school.

04:45.452 --> 04:46.704
Come with me to the teachers' office.

04:48.038 --> 04:48.872
Class dismissed.

04:49.915 --> 04:51.583
Why me?

04:55.963 --> 04:58.424
EPISODE 2

05:17.985 --> 05:18.819
Sir.

05:20.529 --> 05:24.199
I really didn't film you.

05:24.908 --> 05:25.743
PHOTO GALLERY

05:25.826 --> 05:26.744
See for yourself.

05:26.827 --> 05:28.996
This is my video folder.

05:29.079 --> 05:31.415
And this is my recently deleted folder.

05:31.498 --> 05:32.833
See, it's empty.

05:34.501 --> 05:35.335
See?

05:40.299 --> 05:41.759
Is that not why I'm here?

05:43.719 --> 05:47.347
Is it because
I came into the homeroom after you?

05:50.225 --> 05:51.393
Then…

05:51.477 --> 05:52.728
His pride in math is unbelievable.

05:52.811 --> 05:54.063
What a nerdy math geek.

05:55.814 --> 05:58.692
If you perhaps heard what I said earlier

05:58.776 --> 06:01.820
I was just upset about my phone, and…

06:06.950 --> 06:08.869
I'm sorry, sir.
I must have been out of my mind.

06:08.952 --> 06:10.746
-How could I have done that?
-Enough.

06:11.497 --> 06:13.248
How could you only get four points?

06:23.509 --> 06:26.470
I don't even want to open my math book.

06:27.262 --> 06:30.015
It's difficult and no fun.
I don't even get the point of studying it.

06:30.599 --> 06:31.767
I just hate it.

06:32.935 --> 06:33.769
Difficult?

06:34.478 --> 06:35.437
No fun?

06:36.355 --> 06:37.189
You just hate it?

06:37.773 --> 06:38.607
Yes.

06:41.610 --> 06:42.569
What is math?

06:44.238 --> 06:45.906
Math is

06:47.157 --> 06:48.158
math.

06:48.826 --> 06:52.037
How can you be so sure you hate math
when you don't even know what it is?

06:52.496 --> 06:55.290
Math is where philosophy has blossomed.
And what is philosophy?

06:56.291 --> 06:57.918
It's thinking precisely.

06:58.877 --> 06:59.837
Thinking!

06:59.920 --> 07:02.131
Why do mathematicians prove things
through logic?

07:02.214 --> 07:03.799
Why are numbers the root of everything?

07:03.882 --> 07:05.217
Have you considered such things?

07:05.884 --> 07:08.137
-No.
-Exactly. So how can you say you hate it?

07:11.890 --> 07:13.684
So, to reflect on your ignorance of math

07:13.767 --> 07:16.395
and reconsider its origins,

07:17.771 --> 07:19.690
I want you to write a letter to Euclid.

07:19.773 --> 07:21.608
Twenty pages. By the final bell tomorrow.

07:22.484 --> 07:23.360
Twenty pages?

07:23.443 --> 07:24.695
Go. And send Choi Ji-a in.

07:25.821 --> 07:26.947
But, sir!

07:31.201 --> 07:32.035
Yes, sir.

07:46.091 --> 07:47.426
Thank you.

07:48.218 --> 07:49.428
What's your next class?

07:53.557 --> 07:55.309
-Hello.
-Good morning.

07:58.187 --> 08:01.481
I'm sorry about Mr. Ga
having a go at you earlier.

08:02.316 --> 08:04.526
He can be a bit prickly at times.

08:05.444 --> 08:07.696
Sometimes he can be childish and immature,

08:08.322 --> 08:09.990
but he's not a bad guy at heart.

08:11.658 --> 08:12.492
I see.

08:12.576 --> 08:13.994
Sir, that's not the issue here.

08:14.077 --> 08:17.789
You're being gaslit right now.

08:17.873 --> 08:19.875
There's no need to defend him like that.

08:19.958 --> 08:21.501
This is me.

08:22.961 --> 08:24.254
It was nice to meet you.

08:31.678 --> 08:33.096
He's such an angel.

08:34.890 --> 08:37.434
Why does an angel like that
hang out with a demon like him?

08:44.900 --> 08:45.776
Ji-a.

08:48.779 --> 08:49.905
Choi Ji-a!

08:51.031 --> 08:52.157
Hey, wake up.

08:53.075 --> 08:55.827
I said wake up.

08:59.206 --> 09:00.249
Mr. Ga wants to see you.

09:09.508 --> 09:10.801
What did he say?

09:12.803 --> 09:14.429
He wants me to write an essay.

09:14.513 --> 09:15.806
Twenty pages at that.

09:15.889 --> 09:17.307
Because you mocked him?

09:17.391 --> 09:18.308
No.

09:18.934 --> 09:20.644
Because I got four points in math.

09:26.483 --> 09:27.526
Why were you late?

09:28.026 --> 09:30.946
Even if you overslept or didn't want
to come, there must be a reason.

09:35.075 --> 09:37.786
Coming to school on time
is also a kind of promise.

09:43.208 --> 09:44.626
Be on time from now on.

09:44.710 --> 09:46.962
And if you can't, please explain why.

09:47.546 --> 09:49.339
-Yes, sir.
-Off you go.

09:57.264 --> 09:59.516
Oh, you've been lumbered with her, I see.

10:00.309 --> 10:04.730
With kids from the shelter, just be
grateful if they don't cause any trouble.

10:04.813 --> 10:08.400
Don't wear yourself out
trying to establish your authority.

10:08.483 --> 10:10.444
Just get through the year
without incident.

10:10.527 --> 10:11.611
That's your best bet.

10:16.033 --> 10:18.368
CHAPTER 5:
YOU'RE SOFT AND SQUISHY

10:18.452 --> 10:20.996
"Our hall, is a hall of love,
touched by old customs."

10:21.079 --> 10:24.875
"Sun, lower your crystal eyes,
which are like those of a gentle doe."

10:24.958 --> 10:27.919
"And I will smooth my hair,
which is tangled like a lion's mane."

10:28.712 --> 10:31.006
From now on, when I'm with Dong-ju,

10:31.089 --> 10:33.091
the girl we loved back in the day

10:33.175 --> 10:34.593
will be me.

10:34.676 --> 10:36.261
"…before the bright flame…"

10:45.604 --> 10:47.022
Get your hands down sooner, okay?

10:47.105 --> 10:48.357
Eui-ju!

10:48.940 --> 10:49.816
You got this!

10:50.400 --> 10:51.318
Sorry.

10:57.074 --> 10:57.991
Give her a hand!

10:58.075 --> 10:59.701
"Pleased to meet you."

11:00.577 --> 11:01.870
-All right.
-Mr. Noh!

11:02.371 --> 11:03.830
You look like Luciel of Else.

11:03.914 --> 11:06.249
-Right!
-No way!

11:07.918 --> 11:09.920
I was actually scouted
on the street back in college.

11:10.003 --> 11:11.088
-Really?
-Tell us more!

11:11.171 --> 11:12.130
Didn't I tell you this?

11:13.673 --> 11:16.802
-Please tell us!
-Please tell us!

11:17.386 --> 11:18.428
So what happened was…

11:22.015 --> 11:22.974
It comes out like this.

11:23.058 --> 11:25.185
As I said, x minus y isn't zero.

11:25.268 --> 11:27.104
And y minus z isn't zero either.

11:27.938 --> 11:28.772
Try and solve it.

11:35.612 --> 11:37.197
What a jerk!

11:37.280 --> 11:39.366
…the greatest value of x…

11:47.207 --> 11:48.417
Great work today, guys.

11:49.042 --> 11:50.794
-Thank you, sir.
-Thank you, sir.

11:51.837 --> 11:53.004
Where's Choi Ji-a?

11:59.970 --> 12:03.265
She skips homeroom
and leaves straight after class.

12:07.060 --> 12:08.979
Yeo Eui-ju and the next two will clean up.

12:09.563 --> 12:10.480
Why?

12:10.564 --> 12:12.357
-The rotation should start from one.
-Dismissed.

12:12.941 --> 12:14.776
-Thank you, Mr. Ga.
-Thank you, Mr. Ga.

12:17.946 --> 12:20.157
I should've just kept my mouth shut.

12:23.285 --> 12:25.412
That hurts. Can you be more gentle?

12:26.037 --> 12:27.998
How nervous were you to get this stiff?

12:35.797 --> 12:36.631
Hey!

12:40.218 --> 12:41.761
It was so hard writing on the board.

12:41.845 --> 12:43.221
I suddenly stiffened up.

12:43.305 --> 12:44.514
Oh, boy.

12:46.349 --> 12:47.934
How's your tummy?

12:48.018 --> 12:49.227
Okay.

12:50.520 --> 12:51.688
How was your class?

12:52.272 --> 12:53.940
Don't ask. I just want to go home.

12:54.024 --> 12:54.983
That feels great.

12:56.151 --> 12:57.486
That arm is fine.

12:59.112 --> 13:00.280
I'm just touching you.

13:01.031 --> 13:02.616
You're soft and squishy.

13:04.409 --> 13:06.786
"You're soft and squishy"?

13:07.537 --> 13:10.123
Don't you think the female students
are braver than the boys?

13:10.207 --> 13:11.082
Tell me about it.

13:11.708 --> 13:13.001
They were staring so blatantly

13:13.084 --> 13:16.505
I didn't know where to look
and ended up losing my train of thought.

13:17.756 --> 13:18.924
It was so embarrassing.

13:19.007 --> 13:20.675
The mighty Yoon Dong-ju

13:20.759 --> 13:22.719
trembling in front of his students.

13:22.802 --> 13:25.889
-Dude, they'd faint if they found out.
-Let go of me.

13:27.307 --> 13:28.350
Amazing!

13:29.476 --> 13:31.269
Why can't I come up
with dialogue like that?

13:31.978 --> 13:33.480
"You're soft and squishy."

13:34.314 --> 13:36.149
"You're soft and squishy."

13:39.819 --> 13:40.987
Mind your own business.

13:47.702 --> 13:50.455
Why do I feel like such a pervert?

13:56.461 --> 13:57.837
-Hello.
-Hey, you're here.

13:59.214 --> 14:00.048
Are you doing okay?

14:00.632 --> 14:02.634
Sorry for asking to switch
with no warning.

14:02.717 --> 14:03.552
Don't sweat it.

14:04.469 --> 14:06.179
Take this medicine.

14:06.263 --> 14:08.139
My mom gave it to me and it's great.

14:08.223 --> 14:09.474
Thanks so much.

14:10.308 --> 14:11.893
I'll do your shift on Thursday.

14:11.977 --> 14:13.562
It's fine. I can do it then too.

14:13.645 --> 14:15.313
I have something to do.

14:15.397 --> 14:16.773
Okay.

14:16.856 --> 14:17.941
Then I'm off.

14:18.024 --> 14:18.858
Okay.

14:32.914 --> 14:34.708
PAZER WEB NOVEL PORTAL
BEST WEB NOVEL RANKINGS

14:36.126 --> 14:37.294
I'm so envious.

14:38.169 --> 14:39.963
When am I going to see my name here?

14:40.463 --> 14:42.549
I WAKE UP AND FIND MYSELF HIS SECRETARY

14:42.632 --> 14:46.052
"When I opened my eyes,
I had become that guy's secretary."

14:46.136 --> 14:48.388
"Reincarnated as a slave
to an evil family"?

14:48.471 --> 14:50.348
Are regression stories all the rage?

14:51.349 --> 14:53.810
No, I tried something similar
and it was a flop.

14:54.394 --> 14:55.604
Shall I go full on for tears?

14:55.687 --> 14:56.938
Obsession and terminal illness?

14:57.022 --> 14:58.815
College senior and junior?

14:58.898 --> 15:01.610
CEO and secretary?
I've done it all before.

15:04.404 --> 15:05.238
Or…

15:06.573 --> 15:08.074
You're soft and squishy.

15:10.660 --> 15:11.578
Friends?

15:14.122 --> 15:16.207
Childhood friends?

15:18.543 --> 15:19.419
I'm bored.

15:22.714 --> 15:25.884
I'm bored, bored, bored.

15:26.926 --> 15:27.886
Jerk.

15:29.512 --> 15:30.847
Stop it.

15:30.930 --> 15:31.931
Jerk.

15:32.682 --> 15:33.725
The pen's a jerk too.

15:41.650 --> 15:42.942
No, no.

15:43.902 --> 15:45.654
Stop fantasizing about your teachers!

15:46.613 --> 15:47.739
Don't do it.

15:47.822 --> 15:48.698
It's wrong.

15:48.782 --> 15:49.991
I'd like to check this out.

15:56.665 --> 15:57.666
Hold on.

15:57.749 --> 16:01.378
CHAPTER 6:
MY FIRST SNOW… IS A BLIZZARD

16:15.558 --> 16:18.061
Hey, turn that off!

16:18.895 --> 16:20.563
That darn alarm.

16:20.647 --> 16:21.564
Someone wake him up.

16:22.816 --> 16:23.650
Okay.

16:35.328 --> 16:36.371
Hey, Da-ju!

16:37.080 --> 16:38.289
-Noh Da-ju!
-Yes?

16:39.040 --> 16:40.333
Wake up.

16:42.001 --> 16:43.420
Eat your toast while it's still hot.

16:44.587 --> 16:45.630
Is it crispy?

16:45.714 --> 16:46.673
Hurry up!

16:51.177 --> 16:53.304
Is that an alarm or a siren?

16:53.388 --> 16:54.514
Turn it down a bit.

16:54.597 --> 16:56.558
You ignore it every morning.

16:57.934 --> 16:59.185
It's not crispy.

16:59.269 --> 17:01.855
You should have toasted it more. Crispier!

17:01.938 --> 17:03.148
Then don't eat it.

17:03.231 --> 17:05.150
What's with the racket every morning?

17:05.233 --> 17:06.693
What's the key to living together?

17:06.776 --> 17:08.820
Don't disturb your roommates.
It's common sense.

17:10.113 --> 17:12.198
I can't even have an alarm
in my own house?

17:13.324 --> 17:14.659
Can I have your attention, please?

17:14.743 --> 17:15.994
You're my tenants.

17:16.077 --> 17:18.079
This kind of attitude is problematic.

17:20.331 --> 17:22.333
You should be more considerate of me.

17:23.376 --> 17:25.712
You've got the biggest room.

17:25.795 --> 17:28.214
Whenever something happens,
it's "tenant this, tenant that."

17:28.298 --> 17:30.008
Isn't that a crappy thing to do?

17:30.091 --> 17:31.301
-I'm off.
-Crappy?

17:31.384 --> 17:32.927
Did you just call me crappy?

17:33.011 --> 17:34.304
Finish your breakfast!

17:34.387 --> 17:36.681
You carpool with me every morning.
Pay for it.

17:36.765 --> 17:40.101
What the heck? Your car's a junk.

17:40.185 --> 17:42.896
-We're leaving in ten so hurry up and eat.
-Pay me 50 million won.

17:42.979 --> 17:45.231
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

17:45.315 --> 17:48.234
The crags and oceans in this poem,

17:48.318 --> 17:50.737
what do you think they mean?

17:50.820 --> 17:52.530
Literally, they just mean
mountain and sea.

17:52.614 --> 17:53.490
But here…

17:53.573 --> 17:55.784
CHARACTERS
KOREAN LITERATURE

17:56.451 --> 17:57.285
Right.

17:59.162 --> 18:00.914
SONG OF THE GREEN MOUNTAIN

18:00.997 --> 18:03.917
Also, the word night in verse four,
and stone in verse five.

18:04.542 --> 18:07.295
DEPENDENT

18:07.378 --> 18:08.630
Has a dependent personality.

18:08.713 --> 18:11.090
Bit of a pushover. Doe-eyed.

18:11.174 --> 18:13.009
KOREAN LITERATURE
DEPENDENT, PUSHOVER, DOE-EYED

18:14.719 --> 18:17.096
We use these words all the time.

18:17.180 --> 18:20.975
But in this poem,
they all have separate other meanings.

18:21.059 --> 18:23.728
Let's leave it here for today. Well done.

18:23.812 --> 18:25.230
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

18:25.313 --> 18:26.689
Watch and learn.

18:33.738 --> 18:34.948
Mr. Yoon!

18:36.199 --> 18:37.200
Yes?

18:37.283 --> 18:39.619
I got you a chalk holder.

18:40.203 --> 18:44.290
Since we still use blackboards, I thought
you might get chalk on your hands.

19:00.306 --> 19:01.432
Thank you.

19:10.984 --> 19:11.901
Go-ya?

19:13.778 --> 19:14.612
Yes?

19:15.655 --> 19:16.781
Thanks for this.

19:23.705 --> 19:24.706
Hey.

19:28.042 --> 19:30.003
Why? What's wrong?

19:31.296 --> 19:32.130
I think

19:32.964 --> 19:34.883
I'm up against a formidable opponent.

19:37.010 --> 19:38.052
My first snow…

19:39.804 --> 19:40.763
is a blizzard.

20:09.709 --> 20:10.793
Loyal, dependable type.

20:10.877 --> 20:13.004
Beefcake with a bulldozer personality.

20:14.923 --> 20:18.426
Reticent but sweet to his man.
An obsessive top.

20:20.678 --> 20:22.764
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

20:22.847 --> 20:24.140
Good morning.

20:24.223 --> 20:27.060
Today, you'll be doing a long-distance run
for the basic fitness test.

20:27.810 --> 20:28.686
Five laps.

20:28.770 --> 20:29.896
-No way!
-Mr. Jung!

20:29.979 --> 20:31.689
The quicker you run,
the more you can rest.

20:31.773 --> 20:33.274
Line up in rows of twelve.

20:33.358 --> 20:34.692
-No way.
-Sir!

20:35.902 --> 20:37.487
Ready!

21:00.969 --> 21:04.222
CRUSH THE CSAT

21:12.146 --> 21:13.314
I'm just touching you.

21:15.525 --> 21:16.693
You're soft and squishy.

21:21.990 --> 21:23.116
What are you doing?

21:23.199 --> 21:24.534
Put some effort in! You got this!

21:24.617 --> 21:26.285
Faster! Move!

21:26.369 --> 21:27.996
Run! You got this!

21:28.079 --> 21:29.247
Faster!

21:29.956 --> 21:30.999
Come on! Faster!

21:36.462 --> 21:37.338
Faster!

21:38.297 --> 21:39.382
Harder!

21:39.465 --> 21:40.800
Faster!

21:54.647 --> 21:55.898
Stop it, Eui-ju!

21:55.982 --> 21:57.191
No!

21:57.275 --> 21:58.568
Stop it!

22:05.241 --> 22:06.075
That's it!

22:30.600 --> 22:32.060
Whoever wins, I don't care!

22:34.062 --> 22:34.937
Are you okay?

22:40.359 --> 22:41.360
I asked if you're okay.

22:43.905 --> 22:45.573
Yes, I'm fine.

22:48.576 --> 22:49.744
Are you a runner?

22:52.455 --> 22:53.331
No.

22:56.167 --> 22:57.585
Want to join after-school sports?

22:58.461 --> 23:01.672
Give it a shot. Wednesdays at five.
We'll focus on the practical exam.

23:01.756 --> 23:03.966
Drop by my office later
for an application form.

23:07.720 --> 23:09.138
You have real talent.

23:13.601 --> 23:16.729
Sir, I'm going to go wash my face.

23:34.622 --> 23:36.833
You're crazy.

23:36.916 --> 23:38.459
Why is my heart beating so fast?

23:39.961 --> 23:41.087
No way.

23:42.421 --> 23:43.381
You have real talent.

23:45.174 --> 23:46.509
No.

23:46.592 --> 23:47.677
It can't be!

23:47.760 --> 23:50.638
It's beating like that thinking of him
as a character in a novel.

23:52.140 --> 23:53.182
That's all.

23:57.228 --> 24:01.065
CHAPTER 7:
WE WERE FRIENDS

24:01.149 --> 24:03.609
CHARACTERS
KOREAN LITERATURE: DEPENDENT PERSONALITY

24:03.693 --> 24:06.195
PE: LOYAL AND DEPENDABLE TYPE

24:14.787 --> 24:17.832
But there's no obstacle
standing in their way.

24:18.749 --> 24:21.878
Do I need a third guy?

24:21.961 --> 24:24.463
PE, KANG TAE-HA
KOREAN LITERATURE, CHOI YOON

24:24.547 --> 24:27.049
Han Jae-min, who studied abroad,
as the third wheel?

24:28.009 --> 24:29.010
No.

24:29.093 --> 24:30.678
He's too lightweight.

24:34.432 --> 24:37.143
He can be a bit prickly at times.

24:37.226 --> 24:39.270
Sometimes he can be childish and immature,

24:39.896 --> 24:42.231
but he's not a bad guy at heart.

24:42.315 --> 24:43.858
If any footage of this turns up online,

24:43.941 --> 24:46.777
I'll make you regret it.

24:49.989 --> 24:51.073
A regretful top?

24:54.118 --> 24:57.455
The kind that acts like an asshole
and later regrets it?

24:57.538 --> 24:58.372
That's him to a tee.

24:59.165 --> 25:01.459
The asshole of a math genius

25:01.542 --> 25:05.504
turned down offers of professorship
from every Ivy League school.

25:06.297 --> 25:07.798
Why would he do that?

25:08.382 --> 25:11.010
To go to college with his buddy
who majored in Korean literature?

25:11.093 --> 25:13.512
He treated him badly
but secretly liked him?

25:14.972 --> 25:16.224
So, is this how it goes?

25:16.807 --> 25:20.519
The Korean teacher had a crush on the math
teacher ever since they were little.

25:20.603 --> 25:22.897
Attracted by his bad boy charm.

25:22.980 --> 25:25.608
Seeing that,
the PE teacher had his heart broken.

25:26.359 --> 25:29.820
Math, never realizing how much he cared
for Korean, treated him terribly,

25:29.904 --> 25:32.573
and didn't realize his true feelings
until it was too late.

25:32.657 --> 25:36.619
Not wanting to admit it,
he deliberately avoids Korean…

25:36.702 --> 25:40.248
But then PE comes back
as an obsessive top.

25:40.331 --> 25:44.794
Regretful Math clings to Korean,
trying to win him back! Cue tears!

25:48.464 --> 25:49.590
Amazing!

25:49.674 --> 25:51.467
This dynamic is amazing.

25:51.550 --> 25:52.426
This ship…

25:54.303 --> 25:55.513
will sail.

25:57.139 --> 25:59.141
WE WERE FRIENDS
EPISODE 1

25:59.225 --> 26:00.476
IMUK

26:00.559 --> 26:04.522
AS DAWN BEGAN TO BREAK…

26:05.690 --> 26:08.693
AS USUAL, CHOI YOON WAS THE FIRST TO WAKE

26:09.777 --> 26:11.904
SEEING YOON SOBBING,
TAE-HA CAN'T HOLD BACK

26:11.988 --> 26:12.989
Are you dumb?

26:13.614 --> 26:14.907
Huh?

26:17.576 --> 26:20.288
What's so great about that asshole
who always treats you badly?

26:21.747 --> 26:23.874
He can be a bit prickly at times.

26:24.750 --> 26:26.794
Sometimes he can be childish and immature,

26:26.877 --> 26:28.462
but he's not a bad guy at heart.

26:29.839 --> 26:32.717
He's not doing it deliberately,
so don't get the wrong idea.

26:34.760 --> 26:36.304
HE'S JUST USING YOU

26:38.347 --> 26:40.099
He's just using you.

26:41.183 --> 26:43.561
He knows you're kind,
so he just does whatever he wants.

26:47.064 --> 26:48.190
I don't care.

26:50.234 --> 26:53.321
Still, you're the only one
who worries about me.

26:54.447 --> 26:56.324
You're a great friend, Tae-ha.

26:58.284 --> 26:59.285
Friend?

27:00.119 --> 27:02.538
Yeah, my best friend.

27:02.621 --> 27:04.081
YOON'S EYES CRINKLE AS HE SMILES

27:04.165 --> 27:05.583
That made me mad.

27:05.666 --> 27:07.126
Like you were telling me

27:07.209 --> 27:09.378
to keep my distance.

27:18.971 --> 27:19.930
TAE-HA PUSHES YOON AWAY

27:20.014 --> 27:21.140
What about Ju Si-on?

27:22.683 --> 27:23.601
What is he to you?

27:23.684 --> 27:26.354
TAE-HA'S VOICE TREMBLED
WITH JEALOUSY AND FEAR

27:26.437 --> 27:27.563
Si-on…

27:27.646 --> 27:28.564
CHOI YOON HESITATED

27:36.322 --> 27:37.156
What the heck?

27:37.823 --> 27:39.116
Why is this going so well?

27:41.035 --> 27:43.079
I shouldn't be doing this.
They're my teachers.

27:44.455 --> 27:45.289
No.

27:45.915 --> 27:47.083
No!

27:47.166 --> 27:50.503
It's a novel. Besides, I changed all
their names so maybe no one will realize?

27:52.713 --> 27:56.175
I've never written so seamlessly.
The characters, the dialogue…

27:59.345 --> 28:01.180
Still, this is wrong.

28:01.972 --> 28:04.225
What if someone finds out?

28:04.308 --> 28:08.020
SUBMIT A NEW PROJECT

28:17.571 --> 28:19.073
SUBMIT A NEW PROJECT

28:29.166 --> 28:30.960
But my writing is so good.

28:32.461 --> 28:34.755
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 1

28:36.257 --> 28:37.716
SAVE DRAFT

28:37.800 --> 28:38.843
Hey, Yoon!

28:55.484 --> 28:56.569
What are you doing here?

28:57.611 --> 28:59.905
I thought you wanted
to take Discrete Math together.

29:00.656 --> 29:02.116
Yeah, let's go.

29:14.253 --> 29:15.337
Stay away!

29:42.031 --> 29:44.408
BEYOND EUI-JU'S IMAGINATION
TAE-HA, YOON AND THEN…

29:54.502 --> 29:55.544
Okay, let's go!

29:59.590 --> 30:01.175
What's going on?

30:01.258 --> 30:03.511
AND HAN JAE-MIN

31:01.860 --> 31:03.862
Subtitle: Paul Carver
